; The suite of weft-tls on the simulator world (design section 2.19). As
; test/flow, it links windtrap and thus unix. The test code must not call
; Unix. It starts no OS domain, so a mutation run can fork it. FreeBSD and
; Windows in CI have no tls, thus weft-tls is not available there, and the
; build_if skips the suite. An enabled_if with %{lib-available:...} does not
; skip a test stanza (dune 3.23).

(test
 (name test_tls)
 (package weft-tls)
 (build_if %{lib-available:weft-tls})
 (libraries
  weft
  weft.sim
  weft.flow
  weft-tls
  windtrap
  tls
  x509
  domain-name
  ipaddr
  mirage-crypto-rng
  ptime))
